    "narrative": "The LawDog offensive engine is anchored today by **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.26), our two premier plays. **Dylan Beavers** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez, with a +16% park adjustment and a +10% bump for leading off, creating high-upside potential for stolen bases and runs. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo** faces the contact-heavy Miles Mikolas; the combination of a +17% SP Skill boost and an aggressive #2 lineup spot makes him a high-efficiency anchor for our 5x5 metrics. **Bryce Harper** (68.70) remains a mandatory start against Will Warren, supported by an elite xwOBA of .381 and a prime #3 hole assignment, while **Taylor Ward** (64.26) provides strong secondary support alongside **Dylan Beavers** in the same favorable park environment.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical challenges, most notably the precarious matchup for **Cal Raleigh** (43.30). Facing an elite arm in Jacob deGrom (3.07 xERA) forces his score well below our typical starting floor; he remains in the lineup only due to the structural scarcity of his position. Conversely, the most difficult bench decision involved **Daulton Varsho** (46.21). While **Daulton Varsho** gained a +2% boost from a favorable stolen base matchup against an opposing pitcher with slow delivery, his struggle against left-handed pitching and a -10% platoon penalty kept him on the pine in favor of **Gavin Sheets** (55.74), whose platoon advantage against Janson Junk offers a higher ceiling. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Bryce Harper**, **Luis Arraez**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **JJ Bleday**, and **Masyn Winn**; should these projected batting orders shift downward, we may see further volatility in our daily efficiency. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (53.36) also carries some risk today, as his matchup against Rasmussen is hampered by a significant -15% SP Skill drag, making him a marginal play compared to his usual high-output status.",
